The firmware built from it links ESPHome's C++ runtime, which is GPL-3.0, so a compiled firmware image as a whole is
covered by the GPL-3.0: whoever distributes one must make its corresponding source available under the GPL-3.0's terms.

Libraries the firmware is built with (fetched at build time, not copied here):
  ESPHome (https://esphome.io): C++ GPLv3, Python MIT.
  LVGL (https://lvgl.io): MIT.
  ArduinoJson (https://arduinojson.org): MIT.
  pngle (https://github.com/kikuchan/pngle): MIT.
  JPEGDEC (https://github.com/bitbank2/JPEGDEC): Apache-2.0.
  Roboto and Roboto Condensed (Google Fonts): SIL Open Font License 1.1.

The RTL-SDR stick's registers and their values (components/skyscope/rtlsdr.cpp) are those the osmocom rtl-sdr project
(https://osmocom.org/projects/rtl-sdr) found and documented; the code that writes them is this project's own. The Mode S
and ADS-B decoding follows ICAO's published standards as set out in "The 1090 Megahertz Riddle" (Junzi Sun), whose
example messages the tests read.

The LCD 2.8B's panel setup (boards/waveshare-lcd-28b.yaml: its register values, pins and timings) is that of Waveshare's
demo for the board (ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-2.8B-Demo); the driver that sends it (components/rgb_panel) is this project's own.

Copied here: boards/esp-hosted/network_adapter_esp32c6-*.bin, Espressif's ESP-Hosted firmware for an ESP32-C6
(https://github.com/espressif/esp-hosted-mcu), Apache-2.0, as ESPHome builds and publishes it
(https://github.com/esphome/esp-hosted-firmware), unchanged. The P4 board's firmware carries it for its Wi-Fi chip.

Data the screen downloads at run time belongs to its providers and comes under their terms (README.md, "Data sources").
